  "title": "Topological Coherence for Self-evolving Multi-agent Systems",
  "summary": "Topological Coherence for Self-evolving Multi-agent Systems introduces TOCOMAS, a framework that addresses the complex interactions between task regions, agent responsibility, collaboration, and memory boundaries. It enables the optimization of agent and communication structures while maintaining consistency with task dependencies through coupling changes to policy parameters.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "TOMCAS grounds a task graph in tool interfaces, organizes compatible task nodes into reusable responsibility domains, and derives dependency-induced and profile-conditioned collaboration together with boundary-regulated memory visibility.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "TOMCAS proposes coupled changes to agent, collaboration, and memory policies, retaining for subsequent tasks only candidates that satisfy structural constraints and improves evaluated reward.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "TOMCAS improves task success over baselines across backbones in BBEH, WorkBench, SWE-Bench-Verified, and CoMemBench.",
      "confidence": 0.95
